A||||2||terryk||GETRAG BELLHOUSING - Quad 4 vs V6 - ???||||1||
Z||000000||terryk||04-09-2000||12:36 AM||||Does any one know the specific difference in the bellhousings on the Getrag between the Quad 4 and V6 versions?<P>People say they are different, but I see no difference at all.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 04-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodney||04-09-2000||08:47 AM||||Bolt pattern is different and will not bolt up to a 4 or 6. I have never put one to an engine to see the diffreences. I have been told they do not swap.<P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||04-09-2000||10:01 AM||||Since I have both, I guess I can answer.<P>The main difference is where the starter motor bolts on.  On the Q4 it bolts up by the cylinders so the bell housing is narrower at that location.  <P>The V6 (and the 2.5 L4) bolts below the oil pan bolt on surface and since the V6 is wider, the starter bolts on further out thus the bell housing is wider.<P>You can swap the bell housings between the transaxles and get the Q4 transaxle (with the Fiero's bell housing) to work in a Fiero.  You would still need Rodney's adapter kit to make the shift mechnism work since the shifter shaft on the FWD transaxles is 11 MM shorter then the Fiero's.<P>Paul<BR>88 Coupe w/HO Quad 4 <BR>88 Formula w/stock 2.8 <BR>88 GT w/HO 3.1<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
